Wire F-barES-FEM-T4 (U2 + U3) into ccx, and give U5 a null variant.

Adds the two elements of Onishi, Iida & Amaya, Int. J. Comput. Methods
15(7) 1845003 (2018) as ccx user elements, one per EDGE smoothing domain
per material:

  U2  deviatoric   V_h Bt^T D_dev Bt                    eqs. (1), (4), (13)
  U3  volumetric   (K V_h) tbar^T sbar                  eqs. (6)-(11), (17)

sbar is the c-time cyclically smoothed divergence and tbar the unsmoothed
one, so U3's matrix is NOT symmetric.  That half of the wiring is patch
0010; this patch is the elements, the dispatchers and the build.

  elements_ccx/u2edge.f          edge-ring geometry: V_h and gt
  elements_ccx/u3vol.f           the eq. (6)-(8) chain as a row walk;
                                 returns V_h, sbar, tbar and K V_h
  elements_ccx/e_c3d_u2.f        U2 stiffness
  elements_ccx/e_c3d_u3.f        U3 stiffness (raises nasym when c > 0)
  elements_ccx/resultsmech_u2.f  U2 internal forces
  elements_ccx/resultsmech_u3.f  U3 internal forces
  elements_ccx/fbares.py         the deck generator
  e_c3d_u.f / resultsmech_u.f    dispatcher branches for '2' and '3'
  mastruct.c / mastructcs.c      "2" and "3" added to the user-element list
  Makefile.inc                   the six new sources

STIFFNESS AND FORCES SHARE THEIR GEOMETRY.  e_c3d_u2 and resultsmech_u2 go
through the same u2edge call; e_c3d_u3 and resultsmech_u3 through the same
u3vol call, and resultsmech_u3 re-reads the same CCX_FBAR_C.  Patch 0002
records what splitting them costs: an equilibrium_gap of 1.0 and a reaction
cross-check that stops meaning anything.

U5Z -- A NULL BASE TET.

F-barES-FEM-T4 replaces the tet stiffness entirely.  U2 and U3 carry all of
it and both read their geometry from the tets through the 'U5' node->element
map, so the tets must stay in the model and contribute nothing.  The
generator retypes them to U5Z and e_c3d_u5/resultsmech_u5 return on suffix
Z.  It is a deck-level switch on purpose: an environment variable would
also null the tets of a nodal-B-bar (U5+U6) deck, where U5 carries the
deviatoric itself and zeroing it is catastrophic.  lakon(1:2) is still 'U5',
which is what u2edge and u3vol look for.

NO ELEMENT IN AN F-bar DECK CARRIES STRESS.  U5Z is null; U2 and U3 are
smoothing domains with no shape function of their own and write nothing to
stx.  fbares.py therefore drops *EL PRINT / *EL FILE -- left in, they would
report a column of exact zeros as if it were the answer -- and adds a
*NODE FILE if the deck has none.  Results are read from displacements and
reactions.  For the same reason there is no mass matrix and ccx *FREQUENCY
cannot be used, exactly as for U5+U6 (see tests/acceptance_u6.sh); the
zero-energy-mode census runs in the numpy reimplementation instead.

CAPACITY.  The U3 stencil is the full E A^c support and follows mesh
valence.  Measured on the campaign cell LMESH_m0p0240 (117437 soft tets,
184572 edges):

    c = 1   mean 33.7 nodes  p99  78  max 173   ( 519 DOF)
    c = 2   mean 93.6 nodes  p99 259  max 494   (1482 DOF)

c = 1 fits: patch 0008 already carries the user-element matrix at 765 DOF,
which is the encoding limit (255 nodes in lakon(8:8), and userelements.f
refuses more).  c = 2 cannot be a ccx element at all on that mesh.

VERIFICATION (n=6, jitter 0.3, nu = 0.499, K/G = 500; C3D4 is the control)

  patch test, general six-component strain, distorted mesh
    max |u - eps.X| / max|u|      C3D4 3.165e-07
                                  c=0  3.165e-07
                                  c=1  3.165e-07
                                  c=2  3.165e-07
  confined compression, C1111 exact = 2.204400000e+08
                                  C3D4 2.204400e+08
                                  c=0  2.204400e+08
                                  c=1  2.204400e+08
                                  c=2  2.204400e+08
  global force balance |sum RF| / max|RF|   <= 7.1e-15 for every arm

The three arms agree with the control to the last digit printed, which is
this deck's PARDISO round-off floor at K/G = 500, not the elements'.

  zero-energy modes (numpy, clamped-free block, singular values of K
  because the c >= 1 operator is not symmetric): null dim = 6 for c = 0,
  1, 2 at both K/G = 500 and 5000, with sigma_7/sigma_max at the G scale.
  Asymmetry max|K - K^T|/max|K| = 3.3e-02 at c = 1, 2.4e-02 at c = 2,
  2.7e-16 at c = 0 -- the Petrov-Galerkin structure of eq. (17) is live.

